    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Gmail Thread Ingestion Workflow\n\nThis workflow keeps a PostgreSQL database in sync with Gmail threads. It runs on a schedule, pulls new or updated threads, and stores them for downstream automation and analysis.\n\n**What it does**\n* Retrieves Gmail thread IDs using the Gmail API\n* Determines what to ingest based on the last ingestion date\n* Fetches full thread data for each thread\n* Deletes existing records before re-inserting to handle updates\n* Paginates through results until all threads are processed\n\n**Why it retrieves threads that may already exist**\nEmail threads are not static. New messages, label changes, or metadata updates can occur at any time.\n\nTo ensure accuracy, the workflow intentionally re-ingests existing thread IDs. It deletes prior\nexisting records first, then inserts the latest version of the thread.\n\nThis guarantees the database always reflects the current state of each conversation.\n\n**Why it exists**\n* Maintains a clean, up-to-date thread dataset\n* Enables follow-ups, action tracking, and AI processing\n* Supports downstream workflows that rely on email context\n",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        -1344
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "d0013787-d6f9-4914-9a9d-adcb6370003d",
      "name": "Sticky Note6"
    }
